    {
      "id": "hidden-core",
      "cardSha256": "ed9c2df4350546dd3fc20214b3b7eaf036d4503c01a27751bfeb1cc3d5bdb19e",
      "side": "russian",
      "name": "Hidden core",
      "idea": "The east face, two hexes from the flamethrowers and demolition charges, holds only Dummies, three to a hex. The real force stands one hex back: three squads and the 9-2 in the centre, where nothing sees them, and the machine guns at X5, X3, W4, W5, and X2.",
      "givesUp": "Y3, Y4, and Y5 are not defended: a German squad that enters them takes their Control, and the Russians must take back at least one to keep six hexes.",
      "terrain": [
        "The east face looks at the assault engineers' buildings: Y3, Y4, and Y5 see AA4 at range 2, Y4 and Y5 see AA5 at range 2, and Y5 and X5 see Y7 and Z6 at range 2.",
        "X4, the centre hex, has no LOS to or from any German setup Location, nor to any hex next to the building.",
        "X5 sees Y6, X6, and W6 at range 1 and Z5, W7, and X7 at 2, the ground south of the building, and Y7 and Z6 at range 2.",
        "X3 and W4 are seen only from U3 and V2, and X2 from U3, V2, and T4; none of them is seen from the engineers' buildings.",
        "The card makes X3 a Factory (SSR 5), which has no upper levels, so every counter stands at ground level, although the board's data gives the building levels 1 and 2.",
        "The side that Controls six of the building's nine hexes (W4, W5, X2, X3, X4, X5, Y3, Y4, Y5) at game end wins; the Russians Control all nine at the start."
      ],
